    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "288625\nTKA-\n-TWA*",
      "TWA - Transcontinental \u0026 Western Air, Inc.\nBoeing SA-307B-1 Stratoliner\nTWA inaugurated service with the first of a fleet of\nte stratners on july 8th, 1940.\nSoon after\nthe\nJnited States entered World War II, the Stratoliner\nfleet, and its crews, were pressed\ninto service with\nthe U.S.A.A.F.,\nthe\ngiven to the\nmilitary\ndesignation C-75 being\naircraft. Late in the war, the aircraft\nwere returned to TwA, and\nafter substantial modifi-\ncation, were returned to airline service on April 1st,\nThe Stratoliners were\nfinally retired, with a\nperfect safety record, in 1950. The aircraft shown on\nthis card was photographed on February 24th, 1945.\nPublished by Aviation World, Inc., P.O. Box 188, Bethel, Conn. 06801, U.S.A.\n42-88625\nс/п 2000\n(NC19907)\nB-003\n58064-D\npost card\n2002.113.473"
    ],
